From: Davide-F5-Marincione <marincione.1927757@studenti.uniroma1.it>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 16:42:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] KSKA seed expansion: derive
 hybrid-KSK a from a per-key ChaCha12 seed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

KeySwitchGenInternal(priv, priv, ekPrev=nullptr) draws a 256-bit seed from the
Blake2 CSPRNG and expands every part's a component deterministically via
utils/kskseedexpand.h (byte-identical copy of FIDESlib's KskSeedExpand.cuh,
FROZEN SPEC v1: ChaCha12-CTR, domain-separated by (block, digit, modulus,
'KSKA'), exact-uniform rejection with escalation blocks) — directly in
EVALUATION format, exactly what DCRTPoly(dug, paramsQP, EVALUATION) produced
distribution-wise, but reproducible on the GPU from (seed, digit, p, slot).
The seed rides on EvalKeyRelinImpl (m_ASeed, in-process only, not serialized;
OPENFHE_HAS_KSKA_SEED feature macro). u32-moduli chains only; threshold-HE
(ekPrev) and OPENFHE_KSKA_SEED=0 keep conventional seedless keys.
